# ================================================================
# CENZONTLE API — Environment Variables
# ================================================================
# Copy this file to `.env` and fill in the values. Do NOT commit `.env`
# (it is in .gitignore). Full reference for EVERY variable:
# docs/configuration.md
# ================================================================

PORT=3001
CORS_ORIGIN=http://localhost:3000
NODE_ENV=development

# ================================================================
# PostgreSQL (Prisma) — REQUIRED
# ================================================================
# Connection string. With the bundled docker-compose.yml, the dev values are
# user/pass/db = cenzontle/cenzontle_dev/cenzontle on localhost:5432.
DATABASE_URL=postgresql://cenzontle:cenzontle_dev@localhost:5432/cenzontle

# ================================================================
# Encryption at rest — REQUIRED
# ================================================================
# Master secret for the AES-256-GCM encryption of EVERY secret stored in the
# database: the vault's GitHub token, code repo tokens, external secrets and
# the Anthropic API key (OrgAnthropicConfig).
# Any string of at least 16 characters works — CryptoService derives the
# 32-byte key from it with scrypt. Generate one with: openssl rand -base64 32
# The API refuses to start when it is missing or shorter than 16 characters.
# Careful: rotating it invalidates everything already encrypted (you would
# have to re-encrypt).
VAULT_ENCRYPTION_KEY=

# ================================================================
# Auth0 Configuration
# ================================================================
# 1. Create an Auth0 account at https://auth0.com
# 2. Create a new API in Auth0 Dashboard > Applications > APIs
#    - Name: Cenzontle API
#    - Identifier (Audience): https://api.cenzontle.app
# 3. Copy the values below:

# Auth0 tenant URL (MUST end with trailing slash)
AUTH0_ISSUER_URL=https://YOUR_TENANT.auth0.com/

# API Identifier from step 2
AUTH0_AUDIENCE=https://api.cenzontle.app

# ================================================================
# Auth0 — Step-up Authentication (verify-password)
# ================================================================
# Needed to re-confirm the user's identity before high-consequence actions
# (epic sign-offs — the "Dar VoBo" button — both Forge gates and DEV branch
# alignment). Uses the Resource Owner Password Grant (ROPC) against the
# /oauth/token endpoint.
#
# Auth0 setup:
#   1. Create a "Regular Web Application" (not the API).
#   2. Under Settings > Advanced > Grant Types, enable "Password".
#   3. Under Tenant Settings > Default Directory, put the name of your
#      Database Connection (e.g. "Username-Password-Authentication").
#   4. Copy the Client ID and Client Secret below.
#
# IMPORTANT: ROPC only works with Database connections. A wrong password is the
# only case that comes back as 401 (Auth0 answers `invalid_grant`). Every other
# rejection — an SSO/social user, a blocked account, MFA required, the Password
# grant not enabled — comes back as 503 with a deliberately generic message:
# the API logs the real Auth0 error code and refuses to reflect it to the
# client (apps/api/src/modules/auth/auth.service.ts:169-186).
#
# Leave these empty and the behavior splits on NODE_ENV:
#   - NODE_ENV=production → /auth/verify-password returns 503 and every
#     sign-off and gate is blocked.
#   - anything else, INCLUDING NODE_ENV unset → the API logs a [DEV BYPASS]
#     warning and approves without checking the password at all. Fine for
#     local development, a hole anywhere else — set NODE_ENV=production on
#     every deployed environment, or configure the M2M app.
AUTH0_M2M_CLIENT_ID=
AUTH0_M2M_CLIENT_SECRET=

# ================================================================
# Auth0 Post-Login Action
