# ================================================================
# Anthropic (Claude) — NOT an environment variable
# ================================================================
# There is no ANTHROPIC_API_KEY here on purpose. The API never reads the key
# from the environment: OrgAnthropicConfigService queries the database only
# and throws when nothing is stored. Putting the key in this file has NO
# effect.
#
# Paste it in the UI instead — Settings ("Configuración") → Automatización →
# "Anthropic API Key" (/factory/settings?section=anthropic-key). It is stored
# encrypted with VAULT_ENCRYPTION_KEY and handed to each worker inside the
# claim. Get your key at https://console.anthropic.com/settings/keys

# ================================================================
# Redis — AI proposal caches + rate limiter storage
# ================================================================
# In production with MULTIPLE API replicas, REDIS_HOST/PORT must point at a
# shared Redis: the rate limiter (@nestjs/throttler) keeps its counters there
# so the caps are global instead of per-replica. When Redis is unavailable the
# throttler fails open (it does not block requests).
REDIS_HOST=localhost
REDIS_PORT=6379
# TTL in seconds for the epic proposal cache. The value below IS the code
# default: 1800 (30 min).
PROPOSAL_CACHE_TTL=1800
# TTL in seconds for the story proposal cache. It does NOT inherit from
# PROPOSAL_CACHE_TTL — separate variable with its own, much longer code
# default, which is also the value below: 432000 = 5 days, sized for a human
# review window.
STORY_PROPOSAL_CACHE_TTL=432000

# ================================================================
# S3 / Object Storage (MinIO in dev, AWS S3 / R2 in prod)
# ================================================================
# The backend uses S3 (or any S3-compatible API) to store binaries uploaded by
# admins — today the branding assets (logo, favicon), later project documents.
#
# LOCAL DEV (MinIO in a container, via docker-compose.yml):
#   - Bring it up with: `docker compose up minio minio-init`
#   - MinIO console: http://localhost:9001 (user/pass = cenzontle/cenzontle_dev)
#   - The `minio-init` service creates the `cenzontle-documents` bucket for you.
#
# PRODUCTION:
#   - AWS S3: leave `S3_ENDPOINT` empty and set the right `S3_REGION`.
#   - Cloudflare R2: `S3_ENDPOINT=https://<accountid>.r2.cloudflarestorage.com`
#                    and `S3_REGION=auto`.
#   - Any S3-compatible provider: point `S3_ENDPOINT` at it.
#
# `S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE` auto-detects to `true` when `S3_ENDPOINT` contains
# "localhost" (MinIO needs it). Leave it unset for AWS S3.
#
# With NODE_ENV=production, a missing S3_ACCESS_KEY / S3_SECRET_KEY / S3_BUCKET
# throws at startup and the API does not boot. Anywhere else it only warns and
# uploads fail until you configure them.
S3_ENDPOINT=http://localhost:9000
S3_ACCESS_KEY=cenzontle
S3_SECRET_KEY=cenzontle_dev
S3_BUCKET=cenzontle-documents
S3_REGION=us-east-1
# S3_FORCE_PATH_STYLE=true

# ================================================================
# OPTIONAL — features you can also configure from the UI
# ================================================================
# Knowledge vault backed by a GitHub repository. OWNER, REPO and TOKEN are the
# three that matter — BRANCH is optional and falls back to `main`. Set them and
# a vault named "Default" is auto-created at startup, with the token encrypted
# into the database, so you can drop it from `.env` afterward. The auto-seed
# only runs while no vault exists yet (vault-config.service.ts:101-109): once
# one is configured, these variables are ignored. Also configurable in
# Settings → Integraciones → "Vault" (/factory/settings?section=vault).
# VAULT_GITHUB_OWNER=
# VAULT_GITHUB_REPO=
# VAULT_GITHUB_BRANCH=main
# VAULT_GITHUB_TOKEN=

# Log level (pino): debug | info | warn | error.
# Default: debug in dev, info when NODE_ENV=production.
# LOG_LEVEL=debug

# NEXT_PUBLIC_PROJECT_ROOT — absolute path of the monorepo on the API host,
# used as the working directory of the embedded Claude Code terminal. It is a
# frontend variable: set it in apps/web/.env.local, not here.
#
# The EXHAUSTIVE reference for every variable (worker, DoD verifier, code
# security, factory runtime, and so on) is docs/configuration.md.
